{"raw": {"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor/": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor", "description": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Posted October 15, 2026 Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Doctor of Physical Therapy Program,\u00a0Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences University of Charleston Position Summary: Physical therapy core faculty (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) positions are full-time, benefit eligible, twelve-month appointments reporting directly to the Program Director of the Doctor of Physical Therapy program in the Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences. The performance of faculty will be evaluated based upon the expectations outlined in the Faculty Manual for faculty on the academic track. The positions are considered exempt under the Fair Labor Standards Act and classified as Fl. The principal responsibilities of full-time faculty members at the University of Charleston are outlined in the faculty position description published as an appendix in the Faculty Manual and include teaching, scholarship, professional development, and service to the institution. The core faculty hold the primary responsibility for: 1) establishing and upholding program policy, 2) developing, reviewing, and revision of the curriculum, and 3) ensuring that students are professional, competent, safe and ready to progress to clinical education. Fulfillment of these responsibilities may involve weekend, evening, off-campus, and online activities as assigned. This position may be considered for remote candidates, but periodic travel to Charleston WV will be required. Physical therapy faculty (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) primary responsibilities include teaching assigned courses, nurturing and mentoring students, maintaining an active and productive research agenda, and serving the university, community, and profession. The expected curriculum content areas or specialty practice are assigned and aligned to the respective faculty members areas of demonstrated contemporary expertise. Essential Responsibilities: A general faculty position description can be found in the faculty manual (appendix R). Duties specific to the physical therapy program and expectations for faculty success within the Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences include, but are not limited to: Fulfill all functions of a full-time faculty member as defined in the faculty manual, including participation in service to the University, professional development, scholarship, and innovative teaching. Collaborate with colleagues to develop and implement strategies aimed at enhancing student retention, engagement, and success within the Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, including but not limited to academic advising, mentorship programs, and extracurricular activities. Update and maintain one\u2019s personnel action file (PAF), including annual performance appraisals, goals, professional development plans, teaching evaluations, and peer classroom/online teaching observations. Develop professional self to meet expectations of contemporary teaching, service, and scholarship. Fulfill core faculty standards as established by the Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education (CAPTE). Other duties as assigned. Teach (60% of total workload). Develop and deliver courses in-seat or online as assigned from either home-based or campus-based office. Assess student learning and contribute to program assessment. Hold regular office hours. Service (20% of total workload). Actively seek opportunities to contribute expertise and leadership by serving on institutional, community, and professional committees relevant to the field of health sciences, with the goal of advancing the mission of the university and promoting professional growth within the academic community. Participate in program, school, and faculty assembly meetings, graduation exercises, honors ceremonies, and Faculty Institute as requested. Perform duties relating to academic advising and mentoring. Scholarship (20% of total workload). Develop and implement a structured scholarship plan aimed at consistently producing high-quality blind peer-reviewed outputs including publications, platforms, posters, and/or grants. Qualifications: Earned degree in physical therapy. Earned doctoral degree. Hold active unrestricted license as a physical therapist in an appropriate US jurisdiction and be eligible for West Virginia Physical Therapy License or Compact Privileges. Out of state applicants must obtain a West Virginia license or compact privilege prior to course level teaching assignments begin. Developed or emerging research agenda. Experienced in distance education or equivalent with stable high-speed Internet connection from home office. Ability to travel to Charleston, WV multiple times each year potentially up to 2 weeks in duration to actively participate in onsite curricular elements. Demonstrated contemporary expertise to effectively manage assigned teaching load. Willingness to integrate Pain Neuroscience throughout the curriculum. Preferred Qualifications: Earned PhD or terminal academic equivalent. Eligible for appointment at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor rank. Earned Doctor of Physical Therapy clinical degree. Previous teaching or clinical experience working with student physical therapists or post graduate physical therapists. Recognized as Board Certified Specialist recognized by the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties (ABPTS) or other advanced clinical specializations, fellowships, or certificates. Experienced in course and curriculum development. Experienced in curriculum and program assessment. Possess direct experience and working knowledge of the unique healthcare needs of West Virginia and greater Appalachia residents or other rural health populations. Previous uniformed service. Experienced in direct access clinical practice. Willingness to integrate innovative educational technologies into the curriculum including but not limited to virtual reality (VR) and artificial intelligence (AI). Experience as a licensed professional or as a student in case-based or problem-based curriculum delivery methodologies. Willingness to support and assist with clinical education activities. Willingness to relocate and be full-time on-the-ground at the Charleston WV campus to support on campus learning activities. Interested applicants should electronically submit the documents below to: Steven Lesh stevenlesh@ucwv.edu Cover letter summarizing fit with posted qualifications Current CAPTE formatted CV Names of three professional references with contact information (email address if available) One-page scholarly agenda statement One-page instructional philosophy statement Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology/": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology", "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology Posted September 29, 2026 Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology Department of Natural Sciences,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Department of Natural Sciences at the University of Charleston invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor to teach various biomedical science courses, including Human Anatomy and Physiology lecture and laboratory, in support of undergraduate students majoring in Biology, Nursing, and other Allied Health and Health Science majors. The Biology Program serves students in the following concentrations: General Biology, Conservation Biology, Biomedical Sciences. This nine-month appointment is scheduled to begin on August 9, 2027. We are seeking an instructor with college-level instructional experience who can teach anatomy and physiology content to students with diverse backgrounds and who has a documented record of providing students with innovative and engaging classroom experiences. The successful candidate also will have the opportunity to teach biology electives in his/her area of expertise. Preferred candidates will have experience teaching embryology, developmental biology, immunology, or other biomedical science electives. Essential Responsibilities: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate level in the areas listed above Teach courses face-to face in Charleston, WV and online formats The candidate must be able to communicate effectively and work cooperatively with colleagues All faculty are expected to advise students, serve on university committees, and maintain currency in the field The successful candidate will be encouraged to conduct biological research with undergraduates Other duties as assigned Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Biology or related area is preferred, but MS with exceptional records will be considered Prior college teaching experience preferred Good communication skills are essential Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume/CV, statement of teaching philosophy, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: School of Arts and Sciences artsandsciences@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor/": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Assistant or Associate Professor Assistant or Associate Professor Posted September 28, 2026 Assistant or Associate Professor Physician Assistant Program,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: This Principal Faculty member is responsible for providing instruction within the Physician Assistant (PA) program through classroom teaching, laboratory/clinical skills teaching, student advising, assessment activities, and service to the program and university. The faculty member will actively contribute to curriculum delivery, student success, program assessment, accreditation compliance, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. As a member of the PA Program team, the Principal Faculty member collaborates with program leadership, faculty, staff, students, and clinical partners to support the program\u2019s educational mission and ensure the effectiveness of academic and clinical training experiences. The position also includes service to the program, university, and profession through participation in governance, professional development, and community engagement activities. This is a twelve-month, full-time University salaried faculty position with academic rank (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor) determined by academic credentials, professional experience, and institutional criteria. Essential Responsibilities: Teaching Design, implement, coordinate, assess, and continuously improve assigned didactic and clinical curriculum components consistent with program outcomes and accreditation standards. Implement curricula in harmony with the educational approach of the UC PA program through active course direction and instruction. Mentor, advise, instruct, and evaluate students within areas of expertise and interest. Assure the availability of remedial instruction and implement early intervention plans of action. Maintain the security of student records. Develop test questions and other forms of student assessment correlated to learning objectives. Perform test question item analysis for courses assigned as the course director. Assist with the grading of simulated patient encounters, clinical skills, and other grading as needed. Provide regular feedback to the program concerning student progress and problems. Accreditation/Assessment Develop, review, and revise as necessary, the mission statement, goals, and competencies of the program. Review, update, and follow program policies and procedures. Collectively work with the program to review and revise learning objectives, learning outcomes, competencies, and program goals. Participate in ongoing program assessment, evaluation, and continuous quality improvement activities, including data collection, analysis, reporting, and implementation of improvement initiatives. Participate in the selection of applicants for admission to the PA program. Participate in activities of state, regional, and national organizations to promote a positive image of the PA concept within academic, lay, and professional communities. Represent the Physician Assistant Program through service to the university, school, program, students, and community. Attend faculty, school, and university events, functions, and meetings, as directed. Engage in ongoing professional development through clinical practice, scholarship, research, professional service, or advanced education. Assist with the recruitment, development, maintenance, and evaluation of clinical education sites and preceptor relationships. Maintain NCCPA certification. Maintain an up-to-date curriculum vitae. Complete an annual self-evaluation. Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The incumbent should have the requirements listed below. Required \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in physician assistant studies or bachelor\u2019s degree in physician assistant studies with a graduate level degree in a healthcare-related field. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Current NCCPA certification. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Strong interpersonal abilities with excellent verbal and written communication skills to effectively communicate with students, staff, faculty, preceptors, clinical site staff, and organization administrators. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Ability to maintain confidentiality. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Enthusiasm about working in a collaborative environment. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Self-motivated with refined organizational skills. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated teaching skills. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Commitment to student success. Preferred \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience as a physician assistant (2 or more years). \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience in PA or higher education (2 or more years). \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with accreditation. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with advising students in an educational environment. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with curriculum development. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, learning management systems, and electronic communication tools. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Angie Elkins angieelkins@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-business/": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Business", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Business - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Assistant or Associate Professor of Business Assistant or Associate Professor of Business Posted September 24, 2026 Assistant or Associate Professor of Business Entrepreneurship Program Director School of Business,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The University of Charleston invites applications for a faculty position in Business and Entrepreneurship at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. This position also serves as Program Director for the Entrepreneurship major and is responsible for providing academic leadership, curriculum oversight, assessment coordination, student recruitment and retention initiatives, and engagement with the entrepreneurial and business communities. The faculty member will teach undergraduate courses in Management, Entrepreneurship, and related areas, as well as selected courses within the School of Business core curriculum. The successful candidate will bring expertise that supports the broader management curriculum as well as entrepreneurship education more specifically. The University is teaching-focused and student-centered. The School of Business serves undergraduate students across multiple majors, including Accounting, Business Analytics, Digital Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Financial Planning, Management, Marketing, Professional Selling, Sport Business, Sport Analytics, and Sport Media. Our students come from diverse backgrounds and are primarily full-time and residential. The School is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools & Programs (ACBSP). The position reports to the Dean of the School of Business. Essential Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in management, entrepreneurship, and related business disciplines, including courses related to innovation, new venture creation, business planning, organizational leadership, strategic management, entrepreneurial finance, and business model development. Teach selected School of Business core courses as assigned. Serve as Program Director for the Entrepreneurship major, providing leadership in curriculum development, assessment, strategic planning, scheduling, and continuous improvement. Lead efforts to promote program growth, student recruitment, retention, and career placement. Foster relationships with entrepreneurs, business leaders, alumni, economic development organizations, and community partners. Support experiential learning opportunities, including internships, applied projects, business competitions, community partnerships, and capstone experiences. Contribute to program and course design, development, and assessment consistent with ACBSP accreditation standards. Advise and mentor students academically and professionally. Support student organizations, entrepreneurial events, and co-curricular programming. Engage in scholarly and professional activity appropriate for faculty at an ACBSP-accredited institution. Participate in university service through committee membership and shared governance. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master\u2019s degree required in Management, Entrepreneurship, Business Administration, or a closely related field; doctorate preferred. Demonstrated knowledge of entrepreneurship, management, leadership, organizational behavior, innovation, small business management, venture development, and related disciplines. Professional entrepreneurial experience, startup experience, business ownership, consulting experience, management experience, or significant industry experience preferred. Ability to teach a range of undergraduate courses across Entrepreneurship and Management, including courses that support the School of Business core curriculum. Evidence of successful teaching at the undergraduate level, or strong potential for teaching excellence. Experience teaching in multiple modalities, including in-seat, hybrid, and online formats, preferred. Ability to engage students in experiential learning and professional preparation. Experience with curriculum development, assessment, accreditation processes, or program leadership preferred. Record of scholarly, professional, or applied contributions appropriate to rank. Experience using technology effectively in course development and delivery. Excellent communication, collaboration, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to student success and willingness to actively participate in service to the university, school, profession, and community. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, current r\u00e9sum\u00e9 or curriculum vitae, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Shationya Ralph shationyaralph@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/28030/": {"title": "Annual Fund Manager", "description": "Annual Fund Manager - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Annual Fund Manager Annual Fund Manager Posted September 22, 2026 Annual Fund Manager Advancement,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Annual Fund Manager has overall responsibility for the organization, planning and management of the University\u2019s program to seek annual gifts from alumni, parents, friends, corporations, and foundations.\u00a0 UC\u2019s annual giving program raises over $2 million annually. The Annual Fund Manager reports to the Vice President for University Development.\u00a0 Applicants must possess strong human relations, public speaking, writing and motivational skills and the ability to work well with an established team. Essential Responsibilities: Develop overall short- and long-range plans for annual giving, set goals, and manage the budget for all annual giving activities. Create all the component parts relating to annual giving and supervise the implementation and distribution of such plans and materials. Organize and manage all aspects and segments of annual giving including:\u00a0 direct mail, online giving and personal visits. Recruit, oversee and motivate all volunteers and their activities as they relate to annual giving, and maintain timely communication with those volunteers. Personally solicit leadership gifts from key volunteers and selected prospects. Work in concert with other advancement staff to plan and implement special events. Manage a reporting system to provide analysis of the effectiveness of the program on a weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual basis. Responsible for gift records and acknowledge process of gifts including direct supervision of Gift Processing Specialist. Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Applicants must possess strong human relations, public speaking, writing and motivational skills and the ability to work well with an established team. Bachelor\u2019s Degree 2-4 years of related experience with donor cultivation, stewardship, and fundraising Excellent written and oral communication skills that are effective with a diverse range of audiences including board members, faculty and staff donors, alumni and potential and current donors. Prior experience with Raiser\u2019s Edge NXT preferred. Grant writing experience preferred from private and family foundations. Solid working knowledge of SharePoint and MS Office 365 and an overall aptitude with office technology and software. Highly organized and detail-driven with strong time management skills Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Gail Carter gailcarter@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. \u00a0The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/administrative-assistant/": {"title": "Administrative Assistant", "description": "Administrative Assistant - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Administrative Assistant Administrative Assistant Posted September 15, 2026 Administrative Assistant Facilities Services,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Under general supervision, performs a variety of administrative and staff support duties for the Facility Services department, which require a range of skills and knowledge of organizational policies and procedures. The work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Essential Responsibilities: Coordinates and performs a range of staff and/or operational support activities for the unit; serves as a liaison with other departments and operating units in the resolution of day-to-day administrative duties. Provides administrative/secretarial support for the department/division such as answering telephones, assisting visitors, and resolving and/or referring to a range of administrative problems and inquiries. Schedules and coordinates meetings, events, interviews, appointments, and/or other similar activities for supervisors, which may include coordinating travel and lodging arrangements. Posts, balances, monitors, and reconciles internal department/division monthly ledgers, budgets, and financial reporting system reports; may prepare drafts of budget planning documents; may serve as department/division book holder and/or paymaster; may manage petty cash disbursements and reconciliations. Sorts, screens, reviews, and distributes incoming and outgoing mail; composes, prepares, or ensures timely responses to a variety of written inquiries. Requisitions for supplies, printing, maintenance, and other services. Provides support for maintenance requests, closings, reports, etc. Operate computer programs such as Microsoft Word, Excel, Maintenance software Other duties assigned Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. 3 to 5 years of experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified. Receptionist skills. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Records maintenance skills and database management skills. Ability to make administrative/procedural decisions and judgments. Ability to analyze and solve problems. Ability to maintain calendars and schedule appointments. Knowledge of supplies, equipment, and/or services in ordering and inventory control. Knowledge of general accounting principles. Proficient in Microsoft Office products and/or data entry skills. Organizing and coordinating skills. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Jennifer McCallister jennifermccallister@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/custodial-manager/": {"title": "Custodial Manager", "description": "Custodial Manager - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Custodial Manager Custodial Manager Posted September 15, 2026 Custodial Manager Facilities,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Administers and directs program to maintain campus buildings.\u00a0 Coordinate these activities with other departments to ensure a safe and efficient operation.\u00a0 Ensure that custodial employees have the necessary tools to perform their duties and train and develop employees in their area.\u00a0 Maintains custodial standards to the highest ability deemed by University standards. Essential Responsibilities: Provide managerial oversight to team members (scheduling, hiring, and performance) Requisition custodial supplies and test new products; requisition new equipment and parts as needed Maintains and reviews all records pertinent to custodial operations Maintains and reviews associated manuals to include custodial operation and University regulations Continuously inspect buildings to ensure that cleanliness levels are consistent with University standards Maintains operation in compliance with Local, State and Federal regulation Maintains regular communication with Director to ensure consistent operational functions, i.e. scheduling, project identification and completion, cleaning procedures and personnel issues Responsible for training and development of custodial employees. Ensures overall department training effectiveness. Promote teamwork throughout the department Supervise preparation for special events Perform related duties as assigned Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Five years in a supervisory capacity in custodial or a related field Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license and maintain a valid driver\u2019s license throughout employment Ability to communicate effectively with various customers, e.g., students, faculty, external contacts, and supervised staff Ability to utilize a personal computer Ability to work independently with little supervision Good problem solving skills Productive decision making Ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously Flexible, resourceful, willing to learn / cross-train / teach Receptive to feedback from all constituents Must be a team player Ability to organize and prioritize effectively Capable of\u00a0 lifting up to 50 pounds Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Jennifer McCallister jennifermccallister@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/program-administrative-coordinator/": {"title": "Program Administrative Coordinator", "description": "Program Administrative Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Program Administrative Coordinator Program Administrative Coordinator Posted September 2, 2026 Doctor of Nurse Anesthesia Practice (DNAP) Program Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the Doctor of Nurse Anesthesia Practice (DNAP) Program. This position works closely with the Program Director, Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, faculty, students, university departments, clinical affiliates, and other stakeholders to support the effective operation of the program. The Coordinator plays an essential role in maintaining program organization, student and faculty records, accreditation documentation, clinical and academic scheduling, communication, meetings, and program events. The position requires a high degree of organization, professionalism, confidentiality, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines within a complex graduate healthcare education environment. The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator reports directly to the DNAP Program Director and works collaboratively with the Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, DNAP faculty, university administration, clinical partners, and other individuals involved in the administration and delivery of the program. Essential Responsibilities: The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator is expected to maintain a working knowledge of program policies, procedures, academic calendars, accreditation requirements, and administrative processes necessary to support the effective operation of the DNAP Program. The Coordinator serves as an important organizational resource for the program and contributes to maintaining accurate documentation, effective communication, regulatory readiness, and a professional environment for students, faculty, and program stakeholders. Provide administrative support to the Program Director, Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, and DNAP faculty. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate daily administrative operations of the DNAP Program. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain program calendars, schedules, deadlines, files, and administrative records. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Prepare correspondence, reports, agendas, meeting materials, presentations, and other program documents. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate meetings and maintain meeting schedules for program committees, faculty, students, and other stakeholders. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Record, prepare, distribute, and maintain official meeting minutes as assigned. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with purchasing, invoices, reimbursements, memberships, travel arrangements, and other program-related financial processes. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain office supplies, educational materials, and other program resources. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Serve as a primary administrative point of contact for students, applicants, faculty, clinical partners, and university departments. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain accurate student records and assist with tracking required academic, clinical, and program documentation. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with student onboarding, orientation, registration, graduation, and other progression-related activities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Monitor completion and submission of required student documentation and notify appropriate program leadership of missing or incomplete requirements. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with scheduling classes, examinations, meetings, advising sessions, and other academic activities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support administration and coordination of program examinations and standardized testing activities, including the SEE and NCE preparation processes as directed. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with maintaining student rosters, contact information, academic records, and program progression documentation. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate student communications regarding deadlines, schedules, program activities, and administrative requirements. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain confidentiality of student educational records in accordance with FERPA, institutional policy, and applicable regulations. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide administrative support for clinical scheduling and clinical education activities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain current records related to clinical sites, student assignments, clinical rotations, and required documentation. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with communication among students, faculty, clinical coordinators, clinical sites, and affiliated organizations. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Track required clinical documentation, evaluations, specialty rotations, certifications, and other program requirements as assigned. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with maintaining clinical affiliation information and documentation. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support coordination of student clinical onboarding requirements for affiliated clinical sites. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist the Program Director and faculty with maintaining documentation necessary for continued compliance with the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA) standards and institutional requirements. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain organized electronic and/or physical accreditation files and supporting evidence. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with preparation and organization of documentation for annual reports, self-study reports, accreditation reviews, site visits, and other regulatory or institutional reporting requirements. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Track recurring accreditation, program evaluation, and reporting deadlines. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with maintaining documentation related to program policies, procedures, outcomes, evaluations, committee activities, faculty qualifications, and student progression. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support collection and organization of data used for program evaluation and continuous quality improvement. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain current versions of program policies, handbooks, forms, organizational documents, and other official program materials. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide administrative support for faculty meetings, advisory committees, evaluation activities, and other program committees. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate meeting schedules, agendas, supporting documents, attendance records, and minutes. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain faculty files and assist with tracking required licenses, certifications, professional development, evaluations, and other documentation as assigned. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with faculty onboarding and administrative processes for new faculty, adjunct faculty, guest lecturers, and clinical educators. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support faculty with classroom scheduling, educational materials, examinations, student communication, and program events. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide administrative support for the DNAP admissions process. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Respond to general inquiries from prospective applicants and direct program-specific questions to appropriate faculty or leadership. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with open houses, recruitment activities, interviews, applicant communication, and admissions events. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate interview schedules and prepare applicant materials for faculty review. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain appropriate admissions documentation and records in accordance with institutional policies. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with communication and onboarding of accepted students. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with planning and coordination of orientation, graduation, open houses, student presentations, professional development activities, and other program events. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinate meeting spaces, technology, catering, materials, attendance, and other event logistics as needed. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with student and faculty participation in professional meetings and program-sponsored activities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support dissemination of program announcements, recognition activities, and other communications. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain organized electronic program files and shared drives. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Utilize university and healthcare-system information systems as required for program operations. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain spreadsheets, databases, tracking systems, and reports used to monitor program requirements and outcomes. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assist with learning management systems, student information systems, scheduling platforms, survey/evaluation systems, and other educational technology. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ensure program documentation is appropriately organized, accessible, secure, and retained according to applicable policies. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Communicate professionally and effectively with students, faculty, administrators, clinical partners, applicants, and members of the public. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrate professionalism, dependability, initiative, and responsiveness. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Establish effective working relationships across multiple departments and organizations. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Exercise sound judgment in determining when issues should be referred to the Program Director or other program leadership. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Other duties may be assigned as necessary to support the mission, accreditation, and effective operation of the DNAP Program. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Associate degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant administrative experience. Demonstrated experience providing administrative or program coordination support. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities, deadlines, and competing priorities. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive student and personnel information. Exceptional organizational and time-management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently while functioning effectively as part of a collaborative team. Ability to anticipate program needs and proactively address administrative responsibilities. Ability to prioritize tasks in a fast-paced academic and clinical environment. High level of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong problem-solving skills and professional judgment. Ability to interact effectively with graduate students, faculty, healthcare professionals, administrators, and external stakeholders. Commitment to supporting the mission, goals, and continuous improvement of the DNAP Program. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Previous experience in higher education, graduate education, healthcare, or an academic healthcare environment. Experience supporting nursing, nurse anesthesia, medical, or other health professions education programs. Familiarity with accreditation and regulatory documentation. Experience with student information systems, learning management systems, clinical tracking systems, and electronic document management. Experience coordinating meetings, committees, events, and complex schedules. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Megan Orphanos \u2013 meganorphanos@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/international-enrollment-coordinator/": {"title": "International Enrollment Coordinator", "description": "International Enrollment Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / International Enrollment Coordinator International Enrollment Coordinator Posted August 25, 2026 International Enrollment Coordinator Office of Admissions,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Under the direct supervision of the Director of Admissions, the International Enrollment Coordinator has the responsibility for implementing multi-channel marketing and recruitment strategies related to international student enrollment. The International Enrollment Coordinator will be responsible for meeting territory and programmatic enrollment goals through the execution of various approaches, including but not limited to participation in in-person and virtual recruitment events (both on and off campus), and extensive communication with various constituents. Application management and decision making are an integral part of the position. Some nights and weekends are required. Essential Responsibilities: Be knowledgeable about the University of Charleston\u2019s programs, features, facilities, scholarships, and financial aid opportunities. Be able to articulate same in a professional, consistent manner Work with supervisor to understand territorial and programmatic recruitment goals and utilize multi- channel communication strategies to achieve these goals. Evaluate the effectiveness of various approaches utilized Hit enrollment targets weekly, monthly, and annually Manage international application review and associated decision making in a timely manner (typically 1 \u2013 3 business days) in accordance with the goals of the Office of Admissions Interface with University personnel (i.e.: faculty, coaches, deans, support, and administrative staff) regularly Review scholarship eligibility and awards with prospective students Demonstrate strong customer service orientation Be proficient in the use of the University\u2019s management information systems (Recruit and Colleague) and Microsoft Office applications Provide support to broader Admissions Office application and data processing needs Carry out special projects and other duties as assigned Qualifications: This is an entry-level position that requires a Bachelor\u2019s degree Experience in sales, marketing, and/or higher education is preferred Candidate must be a goal-oriented self-starter who can handle multiple projects in a fast-paced environment Candidate must have a reliable car and a valid driver\u2019s license Must be able to lift and carry marketing/promotional materials (up to 30 pounds) Must have excellent written and oral communication skills, strong computer, and organizational skills Be able to think, plan, and execute strategically Candidate must have a customer service orientation and utilize relationship building techniques Additionally, the successful candidate will be a team player who demonstrates flexibility and the willingness to \u201cpitch in\u201d when needed The job will require occasional weekends and holidays Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Jason Sammons, jasonsammons@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/dean/": {"title": "Dean", "description": "Dean - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Dean Dean Posted August 20, 2026 Dean School of Business,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Dean of the School of Business is the chief academic and administrative officer of the School and a member of the University Leadership Team. The position requires an energetic and highly collaborative faculty colleague with a demonstrated commitment to student success, teaching excellence, transformative leadership, and community engagement. This is an on-campus, 12-month administrative appointment with faculty rank, reporting directly to the Provost. Essential Responsibilities: Promoting the University\u2019s values of student focus, quality, and integrity, and its mission to educate each student for a life of productive work, enlightened living, and community involvement Collaborating with University leadership to support institutional and school goals relating to academic excellence, student achievement, enrollment growth, and financial stability Systematically monitoring and assessing the School\u2019s strengths, weaknesses, threats, and opportunities in consultation with faculty, staff, and institutional leadership Continuously monitoring student demand and university contribution for each School of Business academic program Leading planning processes to enhance the academic programs, brand identity and market appeal of the School and the University as a student-centered, teaching-focused institution Partnering with\u00a0University leadership to support School and institutional admissions, marketing, enrollment, retention, graduation, and revenue goals Promoting a culture of innovation, transparency, and shared governance in the School and across the University by encouraging the open, honest, and respectful discussion of issues Ensuring effective communication with internal and external stakeholders in support of School and institutional goals Collaborating with School and institutional leaders to support University academic, athletic, and extra-curricular activities, including interdisciplinary initiatives Increasing graduate and undergraduate enrollment through new student recruitment and returning student retention Growing in-seat and online programs that meet the needs of learners of all ages Collaborating with the School of Leadership which serves adult learners through distance learning leadership and cybersecurity programs Supervising the assessment of academic programs, student learning outcomes, student support services, and administrative functions in the School Facilitating the preparation of School and program information in support of University publications, catalogs, and recruitment materials, including the University website Leading the preparation and administration of budgets for academic programs and administrative functions in the School, aligning budget requests with University goals and priorities Maintaining ACBSP accreditation Practicing data-informed and evidence-based decision making in collaboration with School faculty Recommending faculty and staff appointments, including department chairs and program directors, in consultation with the Provost and, as appropriate, University leadership Supervising faculty and staff personnel issues, including hiring academically/professional qualified faculty, contract renewals, promotions, and disciplinary decisions Monitoring and assessing faculty and staff performance, including department chairs and program directors, on the basis of the University\u2019s personnel policies and practices Identifying and supporting professional development opportunities for faculty and staff, including the promotion of faculty scholarship consistent with University policy Ensuring an equitable workload for staff and faculty, consistent with University practices Advancing the reputation of the School by building community relationships and initiating outreach efforts, including active engagement of alumni, advisory boards, and other professional networks Pursuing external funding opportunities and grant initiatives to promote School and institutional goals in consultation with faculty and institutional leadership Ensuring School compliance with regulatory requirements set by accrediting and governmental bodies at state, federal, and professional association levels Other duties as assigned Qualifications: A terminal degree in a business-related discipline or significant professional experience in a business-related field A minimum of 10 years\u2019 experience as a faculty colleague and a record of progressively responsible administrative appointments in higher education or related fields Documented success in promoting innovation in business education and student success initiatives, including proven recruitment and retention strategies Familiarity with ACBSP or other business school accreditation standards Evidence of strong leadership, interpersonal, communication, and budget management skills. Accomplishments in the areas of teaching, research, and service that would merit appointment at the rank of associate professor or professor Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current CV, contact information for five professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualifications cited above to: Shationya Ralph \u2013 sobusiness@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/feed/": {"title": "Job Postings Archive", "description": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><rss version=\"2.0\"\n\txmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\"\n\txmlns:wfw=\"http://wellformedweb.org/CommentAPI/\"\n\txmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n\txmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"\n\txmlns:sy=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\"\n\txmlns:slash=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/slash/\"\n\t>\n\n<channel>\n\t<title>Job Postings Archive - University of Charleston</title>\n\t<atom:link href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/feed/\" rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" />\n\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/</link>\n\t<description></description>\n\t<lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:47:01 +0000</lastBuildDate>\n\t<language>en-US</language>\n\t<sy:updatePeriod>\n\thourly\t</sy:updatePeriod>\n\t<sy:updateFrequency>\n\t1\t</sy:updateFrequency>\n\t<generator>https://wordpress.org/?v=6.9.10</generator>\n\n<image>\n\t<url>https://www.ucwv.edu/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/cropped-UCharleston-Favicon-32x32.png</url>\n\t<title>Job Postings Archive - University of Charleston</title>\n\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/</link>\n\t<width>32</width>\n\t<height>32</height>\n</image> \n\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:47:01 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=28181</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Doctor of Physical Therapy Program,\u00a0Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences University of Charleston Position Summary: Physical therapy core faculty (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor/\">Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=assistant-associate-professor-of-biology</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:58:20 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=28078</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology Department of Natural Sciences,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Department of Natural Sciences at the University of Charleston invites applications for a full-time faculty position at [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology/\">Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Assistant or Associate Professor</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=assistant-or-associate-professor</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:49:18 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=28061</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Assistant or Associate Professor Physician Assistant Program,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: This Principal Faculty member is responsible for providing instruction within the Physician Assistant (PA) program through classroom teaching, laboratory/clinical [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor/\">Assistant or Associate Professor</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Assistant or Associate Professor of Business</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-business/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=assistant-or-associate-professor-of-business</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:03:23 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=28033</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Assistant or Associate Professor of Business Entrepreneurship Program Director School of Business,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The University of Charleston invites applications for a faculty position in Business and Entrepreneurship [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-business/\">Assistant or Associate Professor of Business</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Annual Fund Manager</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/28030/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=28030</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:15:17 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=28030</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Annual Fund Manager Advancement,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Annual Fund Manager has overall responsibility for the organization, planning and management of the University\u2019s program to seek annual gifts from [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/28030/\">Annual Fund Manager</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Administrative Assistant</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/administrative-assistant/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=administrative-assistant</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:01:47 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=27969</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Administrative Assistant Facilities Services,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Under general supervision, performs a variety of administrative and staff support duties for the Facility Services department, which require a range of [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/administrative-assistant/\">Administrative Assistant</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Custodial Manager</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/custodial-manager/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=custodial-manager</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:00:44 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=27968</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Custodial Manager Facilities,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Administers and directs program to maintain campus buildings.\u00a0 Coordinate these activities with other departments to ensure a safe and efficient operation.\u00a0 Ensure that [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/custodial-manager/\">Custodial Manager</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Program Administrative Coordinator</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/program-administrative-coordinator/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=program-administrative-coordinator</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:33:43 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=27889</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Doctor of Nurse Anesthesia Practice (DNAP) Program Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/program-administrative-coordinator/\">Program Administrative Coordinator</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>International Enrollment Coordinator</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/international-enrollment-coordinator/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=international-enrollment-coordinator</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:00:36 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=27819</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>International Enrollment Coordinator Office of Admissions,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Under the direct supervision of the Director of Admissions, the International Enrollment Coordinator has the responsibility for implementing multi-channel marketing [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/international-enrollment-coordinator/\">International Enrollment Coordinator</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t\t<item>\n\t\t<title>Dean</title>\n\t\t<link>https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/dean/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=dean</link>\n\t\t\n\t\t<dc:creator><![CDATA[carrie stollings]]></dc:creator>\n\t\t<pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:00:02 +0000</pubDate>\n\t\t\t\t<guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://www.ucwv.edu/?post_type=job&#038;p=27772</guid>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<description><![CDATA[<p>Dean School of Business,\u00a0University of Charleston &#160; Position Summary: The Dean of the School of Business is the chief academic and administrative officer of the School and a member of [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/dean/\">Dean</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.ucwv.edu\">University of Charleston</a>.</p>\n]]></description>\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t</item>\n\t</channel>\n</rss>"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-accounting/": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Posted August 20, 2026 Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting School of Business,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: This faculty member will teach undergraduate accounting courses and contribute to the continued growth of the Accounting program. There is potential for program director responsibilities \u2014including leadership in curriculum development, assessment, and community engagement\u2014for qualified candidates. The University is teaching\u2011focused and student\u2011centered. The School of Business serves over 300 business students with undergraduate majors in Accounting, Business Analytics, Digital Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Financial Planning, Management, Marketing, Professional Selling, Sport Business, Sport Analytics, and Sport Media. Our students come from diverse backgrounds and are primarily full\u2011time and residential. The School is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools & Programs (ACBSP). The position reports to the Dean of the School of Business. Essential Responsibilities: Teaching primarily in\u2011seat financial accounting courses, including Intermediate Accounting, Advanced Accounting, and Auditing. Hybrid or online courses may be part of the teaching load as needed. Contributing to program and course design, development, and assessment; mentoring students through organizations and activities; and engaging with community professionals. Academic advising of students. Scholarly activity consistent with expectations for faculty at an ACBSP\u2011accredited school. University service through committee membership and participation in shared governance. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in accounting or related field preferred. Candidates with a bachelor\u2019s degree and significant professional experience (e.g., CPA) will be considered, with the expectation of completing a master\u2019s degree within an agreed\u2011upon timeframe. CPA credential or substantial professional experience as a financial accountant or auditor. Energy, enthusiasm, and excellence in teaching; experience teaching in multiple modalities (in\u2011seat, hybrid, online) preferred. Record of applied scholarship or professional contributions. Experience using appropriate technology in course development and delivery. Ability to engage students in professional and career preparation. Willingness to actively participate in service to the university, school, and community. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Shationya Ralph: shationyaralph@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/lab-assistant/": {"title": "Lab Assistant", "description": "Lab Assistant - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Lab Assistant Lab Assistant Posted August 20, 2026 Lab Assistant Master of Science in Occupational Therapy,\u00a0Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: This position serves as the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy (MSOT) Lab Assistant to the MSOT Program Director, Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, and all MSOT Faculty, both on-site and remote, for the Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences and performs all duties related thereto. The Occupational Therapy Lab Assistant supports the organization, delivery, and maintenance of lab-based learning experiences aligned with the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) Standards for occupational therapy education. This position plays a key role in facilitating student skill development, coordinating with faculty to implement and assess competencies, and ensuring the lab environment supports the program\u2019s curricular goals. Responsibilities also include contributing to course tasks, program evaluation, assisting with events that support student recruitment and retention, and participating in broader university initiatives as requested. Essential Responsibilities: The candidate must have the minimum necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities expected for the position. Organize and maintain a simulated occupational therapy lab for student practice and skill acquisition Prepare classrooms and labs for scheduled instructional activities Assist students with accessing and using equipment and resources during lab sessions Monitor and support safe and secure use of lab space and equipment Track inventory and maintain equipment and supplies; assist with purchasing as needed Complete all equipment safety checks routinely Maintain clear communication with faculty regarding lab needs and operations Support course instructors with skill-based student learning, evaluation, and remediation Recommend additional resources (equipment, software) to enhance lab learning Participate in program-related events such as admissions activities, student orientations, open houses, and all MSOT student events Administer elements of the program\u2019s assessment system related to lab and fieldwork preparation Mentor and support underperforming students through remediation efforts Complete pre and post lab disinfection procedures Assist with fieldwork processes as requested Travel Requirements: Travel to assist with fieldwork site visits, student community service events, and any other student related learning offsite events Physical Demands: This position requires occasional climbing, stooping, crawling, lifting, pulling, and pushing up to 50 lbs. Frequent walking, standing, and balancing is necessary The role demands constant sitting, hand/wrist movements, verbal communication, and near/far vision with depth and color perception Physical strength to exert 20\u201350 lbs. occasionally, 10\u201325 lbs. frequently, and up to 10 lbs. constantly is required Perform other professional duties as assigned Qualifications: Must be an occupational therapy assistant with a minimum of an associate\u2019s degree. Holds and maintains a current occupational therapy license in West Virginia (or eligible). Minimum of three years of clinical experience. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, staff, and external partners. Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency in computer and educational technologies. Commitment to student-centered support and professional integrity. Ability to work independently, demonstrate initiative, and assess operations to improve program effectiveness. Must maintain confidentiality and comply with institutional and accreditation policies. Accommodate a day, evening and weekend lab schedule for hybrid program. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Nicole Scheiman \u2013 nicolescheiman@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-doctor-of-executive-leadership-program/": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Doctor of Executive Leadership Program", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Doctor of Executive Leadership Program - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Assistant or Associate Professor,  Doctor of Executive Leadership Program Assistant or Associate Professor,  Doctor of Executive Leadership Program Posted July 29, 2026 School of Leadership, University of Charleston Position Summary: This graduate faculty member will facilitate courses in the Doctor of Executive (DEL) program, participate in faculty governance, be active in program recruitment, engage in scholarship related to Leadership degree programs, and collaboratively support the mission, vision, and values of the program consistent with developmental, student-centered adult learning principles. Academic rank commensurate with experience. This position is contingent upon the availability of funding. Essential Responsibilities: Facilitate a full-time load in the DEL program Serve as academic advisor for students in the DEL program as appropriate Engage in scholarship in program specialty area and maintain currency and quality of curriculum related to that area Participate in department, school, and University faculty governance Contribute to departmental and program committees, including assessment, curriculum, social responsibility, mentoring, or intellectual community Mentor doctoral students as assigned Collaborate on DEL program and university developmental activities and intellectual community events Attend and participate in doctoral residency Actively participate in program recruitment Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Earned doctoral degree required; leadership-related discipline preferred Demonstrated knowledge of adult learning principles, online facilitation, outcomes-based learning, and assessment Experience in doctoral-level instruction and dissertation committee work Excellent organizational and communication skills, and willingness to work in a collaborative environment Experience in recruitment and building strategic relationships/partnerships Effective inter-departmental collaboration to support program value add and mission alignment Technological competence in word processing, virtual meeting platforms, presentation software, spreadsheets, student database systems (Ellucian preferred), learning management systems Event planning and grant writing experience desired The position requires access to sensitive and confidential student information. Applicant must be able to adhere to student confidentiality policies and procedures Evening and weekend work is required Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Dr. Kristen Dugan: kristendugan@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/administrative-assistant-part-time/": {"title": "Administrative Assistant (Part-Time)", "description": "Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Posted June 18, 2026 Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Provost Office,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant to the Provost is a half-time (20 hours/week), 12-month administrative position reporting directly to the Provost. The staff member in this position works collaboratively with the Provost Office staff, the Executive Administrative Assistant to the President and Provost\u2019s Offices, and other University offices. Essential Responsibilities: Prepare adjunct faculty contracts Gathering of information Mail merge Excel sheet and contract file Upload contracts for Dean and Provost signatures Upload contracts for adjunct faculty signature Create master adjunct faculty sheet Create adjunct SharePoint with Payroll Office/add relevant contracts and master sheet Assist Executive Administrative Assistant to President and Provost\u2019s Offices with faculty overload contracts Course builds for University and Honors programs Assist Associate Provost with classroom assignments In-seat course classroom assignments Requests for day-to-day classroom usage from Athletics and extracurricular groups Provost List Mail merge Provost List letters based on list provided by Registrar Provost List certificates Assist Associate Provost with maintenance of Academic Integrity Violation records Collaborate with Executive Administrative Assistant on maintenance of Provost Office Dropbox Sign Assist Associate Provost with Academic Catalog Prepare payroll paperwork for Provost Office, University Program, and Academic Success Center staff (PEs, TAs, Tutors, etc.) Prepare Dual Role forms for faculty/staff teaching in University, Honors, Innovation and other programs as needed Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred Two (2) years of administrative support or office management experience Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) Ability to work independently and in accordance with University policies and procedures Willingness to take the initiative to create/modify processes to promote productivity Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, including attention to detail Good verbal and written communication skills Ability to maintain confidentiality at all times Commitment to great customer service Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Provost Office provostoffice@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.\u00a0 The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/student-engagement-retention-coordinator/": {"title": "Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator", "description": "Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Posted March 30, 2026 Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Title III University of Charleston Position Summary: The Title III Student Success Coordinator plays a critical role in supporting student persistence, engagement, and degree completion. This position provides individualized outreach, academic and personal support, and coordinates initiatives that strengthen retention and foster a vibrant, inclusive campus environment. The coordinator works collaboratively with faculty, advisors, and student support staff to identify student challenges, address barriers, and implement engagement opportunities that promote a culture of success for all students, including students with disabilities. The position is funded by a grant from the U.S. Department of Education and therefore contingent on the renewal of the award. Although the position is paid with federal funds, the individual will be governed by University of Charleston policies and procedures. Essential Responsibilities: Provide proactive advising and individualized support to students, focusing on academic progress, personal development, and overall persistence. Monitor student progress, conduct outreach, and connect students with appropriate campus and community resources. Identify and address academic, social, and personal barriers impacting student success. Coordinate, implement, and assess retention focused programs aligned with Title III project goals. Plan, promote, and execute campus-wide engagement initiatives that enhance student experience and strengthen student belonging. Support engagement and retention efforts for all students, including students with disabilities. Work collaboratively with faculty, advisors, student support services, and campus partners to maintain a coordinated and holistic approach to student success. Contribute to institutional retention strategies through cross departmental partnerships. Maintain accurate records of student interactions, outreach, and program participation. Assist with data collection, evaluation, and reporting related to retention and student success initiatives. Occasional travel to Beckley campus may be required. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in educational counseling, higher education, or a related field required; master\u2019s degree preferred. Three to five years of professional experience in higher education, with emphasis on student success, retention, support services, or engagement. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships with diverse student populations and collaborate across departments. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive campus environment. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current vitae/resume, contact information for three professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualification identified to: Provost Office provostoffice@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/data-support-specialist/": {"title": "Data Support Specialist", "description": "Data Support Specialist - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Data Support Specialist Data Support Specialist Posted March 30, 2026 Data Support Specialist Title III University of Charleston Position Summary: The Data Analyst supports the Title III project by collecting, managing, and analyzing institutional and project-level data. This role is essential to evaluating project outcomes and informing data-driven decision-making that enhances student success and institutional effectiveness. The position is funded by a grant from the U.S. Department of Education and therefore contingent on the renewal of the award. Although the position is paid with federal funds, the individual will be governed by University of Charleston policies and procedures. Essential Responsibilities: Collect, clean, and analyze data relevant to Title III project goals and institutional performance. Manage databases and ensure data integrity, security, and accessibility. Generate clear, actionable reports and visualizations for internal and external stakeholders. Collaborate with the Office of Institutional Research to align data practices and reporting standards. Support ongoing evaluation of project outcomes and contribute to grant reporting requirements. Other duties assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in statistics, data science, or a related field required, master\u2019s degree preferred. Minimum of 3 years of experience in data analysis, preferably in a higher education or grant-funded environment. Proficiency in data analysis tools such as Excel, SPSS, R, Python, or Tableau. Strong attention to detail, analytical thinking, and communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current vitae/resume, contact information for three professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualification identified to: Provost Office provostoffice@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/barista/": {"title": "Barista", "description": "Barista - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Barista Barista Posted February 17, 2026 Barista Food Service & Catering,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: The University of Charleston is seeking friendly, energetic, and customer-focused Baristas to join our campus Food Service & Catering team. Our coffee shop proudly serves Starbucks beverages and provides a welcoming space for students, faculty, staff, and guests. Essential Responsibilities: Prepare and serve high-quality hot and cold beverages, including coffee, espresso, cappuccinos, lattes, and blended drinks, in accordance with Starbucks standards. Deliver exceptional customer service by creating a warm, welcoming experience for every guest through friendly conversation and efficient service. Greet customers promptly and courteously upon arrival at the counter. Accurately operate a cash register and handle cash transactions, including making correct change. Maintain a clean, organized, and sanitary work environment, including the counter, prep area, and equipment. Demonstrate initiative and creative thinking by suggesting workflow improvements or service enhancements to supervisors. Adhere to all food safety, sanitation, and university policies. Perform other duties as assigned to support daily operations. Qualifications: Ability to multitask and work efficiently in a fast-paced environment Previous barista or food service experience preferred, but not required Strong communication and customer service skills Ability to accurately handle cash transactions Ability to lift up to 40 pounds Reliable attendance and punctuality Team-oriented attitude with a positive, professional demeanor Benefits: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation and Sick Leave Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits at the University of Charleston Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: University of Charleston stanleychamberlain@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/admissions-counselor-undergraduate-nursing/": {"title": "Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Nursing", "description": "Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Nursing - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Nursing Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Nursing Posted February 17, 2026 Admissions Counselor \u2013 Undergraduate Nursing Office of Admissions,\u00a0University of Charleston Position Summary: Under the direct supervision of the Director of Admissions, the Undergraduate Nursing Admissions Counselor has the responsibility for implementing multi-channel marketing and recruitment strategies related to nursing student enrollment. The Undergraduate Nursing Admissions Counselor will be responsible for meeting territory and programmatic enrollment goals for the Charleston BSN, ADN, and Online RN-BSN programs through the execution of various approaches, including but not limited to travel to high schools and college fairs, participation in in-person and virtual recruitment events (both on and off campus), and extensive communication with various constituents. Application management and decision making are an integral part of the position. Some nights and weekends are required. This position reports to the Director of Admissions. Essential Responsibilities: Be knowledgeable about the University of Charleston\u2019s programs, features, facilities, scholarships, and financial aid opportunities. Be able to articulate same in a professional, consistent manner. Work with supervisor to understand territorial and programmatic recruitment goals and utilize multi-channel communication strategies to achieve these goals. Evaluate the effectiveness of various approaches utilized. Hit enrollment targets weekly, monthly, and annually. Participate in tele-counseling with prospective students. Manage application review and associated decision making. Interface with University personnel (i.e.: nursing program faculty, deans, support and administrative staff) as required. Review financial aid packages with prospective students. Demonstrate strong customer service orientation. Be proficient in the use of the University\u2019s management information systems (Recruit and Colleague) and Microsoft Office applications. Carry out special projects. Overnight travel during college fair months. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required for this entry level position. Experience in sales, marketing, and/or higher education is preferred. Candidate must be a goal-oriented self-starter who has the ability to handle multiple projects in a fast-paced environment. Candidate must have a reliable car and a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to lift and carry marketing/promotional materials (up to 30 pounds). Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong computer and organizational skills. Must be able to think, plan, and execute strategically. Candidate must have a customer service orientation and utilize relationship building techniques. A team player who demonstrates flexibility and the willingness to \u201cpitch in\u201d when needed. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: jasonsammons@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/security-patrol-officer/": {"title": "Security Patrol Officer", "description": "Security Patrol Officer - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Security Patrol Officer Security Patrol Officer Posted October 28, 2025 Security Patrol Officer Department of Safety & Security,\u00a0University of Charleston Essential Functions of the Job: Documentation and initial investigation of all reported crime related incidents, car accidents, personal injuries, industrial or employee accidents, suspicious activity, Homeland Security concerns etc. Assist all law enforcement agencies and emergency personnel called upon to assist the university. (Mutual aid agreement in place with local agencies) Accurate documentation of all incidents and activity required by the U. S. Dept. of Education for campus crime reporting purposes. Routine day and night patrols of all campus property (both foot and vehicle patrols). Special patrols and or extra patrols may also be designated for specific locations based on events and activity. Confronting and removing offenders or trespassers from the campus community. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required: Physical Requirements: Walking and/or Running Regularly required to stand; walk; sit; stoop, kneel and crouch The employee is frequently required to use hands to feel; reach with hands and arms; and talk or hear The employee is occasionally required to lift and move up to 25 pounds Employee will be required to work outdoors for extended periods of times with exposure to both hot and cold ambient temperatures Employee may be required take action during an emergency situation to include violent encounters with suspects Daily lock up and opening of university buildings, designated classrooms and offices Parking and traffic enforcement Extra patrol assignments to deal with large events, crowds and parking concerns Special surveillance assignments as directed Daily visual inspection of grounds and buildings during routine patrol to determine any existing fire hazards, safety issues and immediate maintenance concerns to be reported to Facilities Extra patrol at sporting events with escorts for coaches & referees as required by collegiate rules Courtesy calls to assist people locked out of their car, office, with dead car batteries etc. Note: when officers are tied up on routine security functions, courtesy calls will be addressed if and when officers become available Bank escorts for the university as needed Completion of all mandatory security / law enforcement job related training and other training as required Must have a valid driver\u2019s license with no serious traffic offenses in the last 7 \u2013 9 years for the following violations: DUI Reckless Driving Leaving the Scene Hit and Run If not certified, \u2013 eventual certification with the ASP tactical baton, Pepper Spray, Taser, CPR, AED, Basic First Aid and all required levels of NIMS Other duties as assigned Interested applicants send cover letter and resume to: Eric Smith, Chief of Security, ericsmith@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/join-ucs-food-services-team/": {"title": "Join UC\u2019s Food Services Team", "description": "Join UC\u2019s Food Services Team - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Join UC\u2019s Food Services Team Join UC\u2019s Food Services Team Posted September 30, 2025 We\u2019re looking for hardworking, team-oriented individuals to help fuel our campus community. The University of Charleston\u2019s Food Service & Catering Department offers full-time positions with great benefits, plenty of overtime, and tuition assistance for employees and their dependents. Bring your skills or start learning with us, and become part of the Golden Eagle family. How to Apply Ready to join our team? Email your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 or a short note of interest to schamberlain@avifoodsystems.com and we\u2019ll be in touch quickly. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis until each position is filled. Apply Now Current Openings Click any job title to view the full description and apply: Food Service & Catering Assistant Utility Worker / Dishwasher Food Service Worker Grill Cook Cashier Cook Bring your passion for food service and help us make a difference every day on campus! The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-professor-of-nursing-adn/": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing-ADN", "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing-ADN - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Beckley / Assistant Professor of Nursing-ADN Assistant Professor of Nursing-ADN Posted August 1, 2025 Assistant Professor of Nursing-ADN University of Charleston \u2013 Beckley Position Summary: Full-time faculty members teach in the university\u2019s Associate Degree Nursing (ADN) program at the Beckley Instructional Site. This position is a 12-month, full-time position. The faculty member will teach theory and clinical courses and assist in the preparation of students for a life of productive work, enlightened living, and community involvement. This position will be for the Beckley Instructional Site only. The faculty member will be responsible for teaching the didactic/theory and clinical experiences as they relate to the foundational concepts of the course objectives and End-of-Program Student Learning Outcomes (EPSLOs). Essential Responsibilities: Be able and willing to commit and adhere to the policies of the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Science, and the Capito Department of Nursing, but not limited to the following: Full-time teaching assignment in the Associate Degree Nursing weekend (hybrid) program. Maintain a minimum of 5 office hours per week (3 in-seat, 2 online) for advising in addition to on campus office hours as mandated by the Chair, Program Director of Nursing. The designated office hours must be consistent from week to week, and any foreseen variations must be reported/approved by the Chair of the Nursing Department. Display required office hours on door and online for students/advisees.\u00a0 A copy of office hours must be forwarded to the department of nursing administrative assistants, and the Program Director of nursing upon the start of each semester. Attend all functions and meetings scheduled by the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing. Serve on university and departmental committees as assigned. Provide instructional and/or non-instructional services as a member of the nursing team specified by the faculty member\u2019s contract. Actively participate in the development, evaluation and review of curriculum, services, and activities of the nursing program. Actively participate in the self-study and accreditation process for the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and maintain yearly supportive documentation data in addressing standards and criteria. Instruct courses in a professional and ethical manner consistent with the University of Charleston and the Capito Department of Nursing. Utilize resources consistent with the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing as appropriate to enhance learning. Communicate with students, faculty, staff, clinical agencies, and the community in a professional and ethical manner. Commit to lifelong learning and maintain current competency in subject matter and service or clinical area. Participate in scholarly activities, including but not limited to professional development and conferences. Assume responsibility and accountability for instruction, evaluation of students, planning, and implementing curriculum content in the didactic and/or clinical area. Establish effective working relationships with personnel from community healthcare agencies. Assist the students in the identification and understanding of The University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing policies and procedures pertaining to the student, including, but not limited to: Mission and Philosophy Outcomes Student responsibilities and accountability to the University, program, clinical facilities, patients, and accrediting bodies. Learning experiences Curriculum, instruction, and evaluation throughout the program. Maintain a student advising load as determined by the Dean of Health Sciences and/or Chair, Program Director of Nursing. Advising files are to be kept current from semester to semester, and documentation of student contacts/communications are to be placed in the advising file for ongoing evaluation. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: In accordance with the West Virginia Code 30-7-5a titled \u2018Schools of nursing faculty requirements\u2019, in order to acquire a full-time faculty position in nursing, individuals must have a graduate degree with a major in nursing; have a bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and be enrolled in a graduate degree program with a major in nursing within one year of employment as a faculty member; or have a bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and at least 10 years of direct patient care experience; have evidence of current experience in nursing practice and education sufficient to demonstrate professional competence.\u00a0 For part-time faculty, all of the previous requirements apply with the exception that the individual must have a bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and at least two years of direct patient care experience in nursing.\u00a0 Previous teaching experience including proficiency in curriculum development, supervision, instruction, assessment, evaluation and advising in a registered professional nursing program is preferred. Specific requirements are exhibited as follows: MSN required or a BSN and willing to enroll in an MSN program within one year of employment as a faculty member, or a BSN with 10 years of direct patient care experience. Minimum 2 years teaching experience in an RN program preferred. Recent clinical experience required (2 years in the past 10 years) in Medical Surgical Nursing Unencumbered, or ability to obtain an unencumbered WV RN license. Maintain current RN licensure and certifications. Offer of employment pending approval by the West Virginia Board of Examiners for Registered Professional Nurses Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Kennita Thomas kennitalthomas@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/food-service-and-catering-assistant/": {"title": "Food Service and Catering Assistant", "description": "Food Service and Catering Assistant - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Food Service and Catering Assistant Food Service and Catering Assistant Posted June 23, 2025 Food Service and Catering Assistant University of Charleston Position Purpose The Food Service and Catering Assistant will assist with the daily operations of the Food Service and Catering Department, complying with the University of Charleston and AVI Fresh policies and assisting in the achievement of organizational goals. Position Requirements Manages the Food Service and Catering office as the office manager. Manages all check requests and expense reports for both UC and AVI processes. Assists the Director of Catering with event billing when necessary Communicate effectively, verbally and in writing. Leads and assists with set-up, service, and closing of catering events when necessary Ability to lift, carry, or otherwise move objects weighing up to 30 pounds. Works closely with the Catering Director and Executive Chef to organize customer requests, inquiries, and bookings. Uses Excel, Word, and Web-based Catering software daily. Works evenings, weekends, and overtime as needed. Works cashier station as needed. Ability to cross-train in all areas of Food Service. Other duties as assigned. Benefits: Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits To apply for the position, send cover letter and resume to: University of Charleston Attention: Elizabeth Brandt, Food Service 2300 MacCorkle Avenue, SE, Charleston, WV\u00a0 25304 elizabethbrandt@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/sous-chef/": {"title": "Sous Chef", "description": "Sous Chef - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Sous Chef Sous Chef Posted June 23, 2025 Sous Chef (Hourly) University of Charleston Primary Functions: To assist the Executive Chef and Culinary Team in all aspects of the food service operation.\u00a0 To ensure that all company policies and procedures are adhered to and at an acceptable level so that our customers receive the highest level of service and food quality. Position Requirements: Able to read, write, and perform basic math Able to follow verbal and written instructions Exceptional interpersonal skills and decision-making ability Ability to lead, supervise, and coordinate activities of others High standard of personal hygiene Three years culinary experience or culinary degree Operational knowledge of commercial kitchen equipment Typical Duties & Responsibilities: Supervise and assist in the production of hot and cold foods Assist Executive Chef in ordering, receiving and inventory process Keep production records such as par levels, waste logs and temperature logs Menu development and recipe costing Follow standardized recipes Supervision of all staff members Implementation of catered events, promotional programs and new standards Monitors safety and sanitation standards to meet Federal, State and Local laws Other duties as required and assigned Benefits Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits To apply for the position, send cover letter and resume to: University of Charleston Attention: Elizabeth Brandt- Food Service 2300 MacCorkle Avenue SE, Charleston, WV 25403 elizabethbrandt@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/financial-aid-assistant/": {"title": "Financial Aid Assistant", "description": "Financial Aid Assistant - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Financial Aid Assistant Financial Aid Assistant Posted April 22, 2025 Financial Aid Assistant University of Charleston Job Summary: The Financial Aid Assistant is responsible for assisting in the overall operations of the Financial Aid Office. The Assistant is responsible for processing student financial aid applications, answering concerns of parents and students, and performing other duties in support of the operation of the Financial Aid function for the University. Responsibilities also include serving as a receptionist, managing the office, and organizing files for the Financial Aid Office. Position reports to the Director of Financial Aid. Essential Functions of the Position: Provide direct, quick, accurate, and convenient service to parents and students through addressing a range of student financial aid needs that require immediate attention. This includes, but is not limited to, the following functions on an as-needed basis: Assist students with completing the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). Assist students with accessing their tax transcripts and verification documents. Counsel perspective and current students concerning their eligibility for federal, state and institutional financial aid. Counsel students in completing Entrance Loan Counseling and Master Promissory Note (MPN). Maintain accurate student records in the computer and in the files. Answer incoming calls. Track all incoming and outgoing documents by mail, fax or email. Maintain the Financial Aid general email account. Process Financial Aid Award Offer packets for prospective students. Monitor Exit Loan Counseling notices. Make sure all forms are updated annually. Work cooperatively with other offices on campus, particularly Admissions and the Athletic Department. Participate in University activities, e.g., Experience UC Day, Maroon & Gold Day, and other financial aid events. Review and monitor the Transfer Monitoring List and alerts for all transfer students. Assist in monitoring the Federal Work Study program. Assist in the monitoring of satisfactory academic progress for financial aid recipients. Assist in the annual University audit as needed. Assist students in accessing data in the Colleague System. Perform related duties as necessary and as assigned. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Associate degree recommended 2 years of direct Financial Aid experience or 4 or more years of Accounting or other relevant experience Applicable experience and assistant competencies will be considered Ability to maintain confidentiality of information Ability to prioritize and organize effectively Ability to communicate effectively with the various customer bases, e.g., students, staff, faculty, and external contacts Ability to utilize a personal computer and familiarity with Microsoft Office Suite applications Ability to work independently with little supervision Results-oriented interpersonal and organizational skills Knowledge of general office procedures Ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously Flexible, resourceful, willing to learn\\cross-train Must be a team player Other duties assigned Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, a current resume, and the names of three professional references with contact information (including email address if available) to: Christine Tomczyk christinetomczyk@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employe Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/shuttle-bus-driver-athletics-department/": {"title": "Shuttle Bus Driver", "description": "Shuttle Bus Driver - Athletics Department - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Shuttle Bus Driver \u2013 Athletics Department Shuttle Bus Driver \u2013 Athletics Department Posted April 2, 2025 Shuttle drivers are responsible for safely transporting students, coaches, clients and/or vendors. The safety of passengers is the prime responsibility of bus drivers. Shuttle bus drivers are expected to provide a superior, safe service. Individual must have good communication skills both oral and written to interact with fellow drivers, maintenance, the operations team as well as the public they serve. Commitment, patience, maturity, and initiative are required qualities. This is a part-time, temporary, as-needed position with the University. Essential Functions: Drive safely, responsibly and be prepared for all road conditions Respect equipment, students, coaches, fellow employees and relate to all levels of staff and management Follow all traffic laws and posted speed limits Inspect vehicle to ensure that it is functioning correctly (emphasis on ensuring adequate fluid levels) Complete all applicable paper work required Maintain radio contact and use proper radio protocol Fuel bus as required and record information as per procedure No passengers on while fueling Maintain a clean bus Must attend required safety meetings and other training sessions Report unsafe conditions Report an injury Use the safe work procedures Patience is necessary when dealing with heavy traffic Cooperate with the employer through involvement in all aspects of the health and safety management system Preferred Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Candidates must meet state and federal regulations Commercial driver\u2019s license, or CDL Drivers must also obtain a passenger endorsement allowing you to transport people Minimum six months experience as a licensed commercial driver and good driving skills and record Interpersonal skills Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current resume to: University of Charleston Attention: Todd Diuguid 2300 MacCorkle Ave. SE Charleston, WV 25304 todddiuguid@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/nursing-faculty/": {"title": "Nursing Faculty", "description": "Nursing Faculty - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Nursing Faculty Nursing Faculty Posted November 8, 2024 Nursing Faculty Associate Degree Program Capito Department of Nursing, University of Charleston Job Description: Full\u2013time faculty members teach in the university\u2019s Associate Degree Nursing (ADN) program at the Charleston campus and/or Beckley location. This position is a 12-month, full-time position. The faculty member will teach theory and clinical courses and assist in the preparation of students for a life of productive work, enlightened living, and community involvement. This position will be for the Charleston Campus location. This position reports to the Chair, Program Director of Nursing. The faculty member will be responsible for teaching the didactic/theory and clinical experiences as they relate to the foundational concepts of the course objectives and End-of-Program Student Learning Outcomes (EPSLOs). Duties of the Nursing Instructor: Be able and willing to commit and adhere to the policies of the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Science, and the Capito Department of Nursing, but not limited to the following: Full-time teaching assignment in the Associate Degree Nursing weekend (hybrid) program Maintain a minimum of 5 office hours per week (3 in-seat, 2 online) for advising in addition to on campus office hours as mandated by the Chair, Program Director of Nursing The designated office hours must be consistent from week to week, and any foreseen variations must be reported/approved by the Chair of the Nursing Department Display required office hours on door and online for students/advisees A copy of office hours must be forwarded to the department of nursing administrative assistants, and the Program Director of nursing upon the start of each semester Attend all functions and meetings scheduled by the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing Serve on university and departmental committees as assigned Provide instructional and/or non-instructional services as a member of the nursing team specified by the faculty member\u2019s contract Actively participate in the development, evaluation and review of curriculum, services, and activities of the nursing program Actively participate in the self-study and accreditation process for the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and maintain yearly supportive documentation data in addressing standards and criteria Instruct courses in a professional and ethical manner consistent with the University of Charleston and the Capito Department of Nursing Utilize resources consistent with the University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing as appropriate to enhance learning Communicate with students, faculty, staff, clinical agencies, and the community in a professional and ethical manner Commit to life-long learning and maintain current competency in subject matter and service or clinical area Participate in scholarly activities including but not limited to professional development and conferences Assume responsibility and accountability for instruction, evaluation of students, planning and implementing curriculum content in the didactic and/or clinical area Establish effective working relationships with personnel from community healthcare agencies. Assist the students in the identification and understanding of The University of Charleston, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, and the Capito Department of Nursing policies and procedures pertaining to the student, including, but not limited to: Mission and Philosophy Outcomes Student responsibilities and accountability to the University, program, clinical facilities, patients, and accrediting bodies. Learning experiences Curriculum, instruction, and evaluation throughout the program Maintain a student advising load as determined by the Dean of Health Sciences and/or Chair, Program Director of Nursing Advising files are to be kept current from semester to semester, and documentation of student contacts/communications are to be placed in the advising file for ongoing evaluation Other duties as assigned Minimum Requirements: In accordance with the West Virginia Code 30-7-5a titled \u2018Schools of nursing faculty requirements\u2019, in order to acquire a full-time faculty position in nursing, individuals must have the following: Graduate degree with a major in nursing Bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and be enrolled in a graduate degree program with a major in nursing within one year of employment as a faculty member; or have a bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and at least 10 years of direct patient care experience; have evidence of current experience in nursing practice and education sufficient to demonstrate professional competence Part-time faculty, all of the previous requirements apply with the exception that the individual must have a bachelor\u2019s degree with a major in nursing and at least two years of direct patient care experience in nursing.\u00a0 Previous teaching experience including proficiency in curriculum development, supervision, instruction, assessment, evaluation and advising in a registered professional nursing program is preferred. Specific requirements are exhibited as the following: MSN required or a BSN and willing to enroll in an MSN program within one year of employment as a faculty member, or a BSN with 10 years of direct patient care experience Minimum 2 years teaching experience in an RN program preferred Recent clinical experience required (2 years in the past 10 years) in Medical Surgical Nursing Unencumbered, or ability to obtain an unencumbered WV RN license Maintain current RN licensure and certifications Offer of employment pending approval by the West Virginia Board of Examiners for Registered Professional Nurses Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: University of Charleston Jessica Pistner Email: jessicapistner@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/utility-worker-dishwasher/": {"title": "Utility Worker / Dishwasher", "description": "Utility Worker / Dishwasher - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Utility Worker / Dishwasher Utility Worker / Dishwasher Posted May 3, 2024 Utility Worker / Dishwasher Food Services, University of Charleston Essential Functions of the Position: Assists with cleaning the kitchen, serving and dining areas including washing tables and chairs, washing dishes, washing and sanitizing equipment, cleaning the floor and discarding of trash, maintaining sanitary work area Wash dishes, glassware, flatware, pots and/or pans using dishwashers or by hand Stores and stocks supply in a safe, sanitary manner Follow and adhere to all sanitation and safety standards Ensure all kitchen work areas, equipment and utensils are clean, professional and in an orderly condition always Place clean dishes, utensils, and cooking equipment in proper storage areas Ensure the workspace meets or exceeds all established sanitation and safety standards Ability to lift/transport 30lbs Request supplies and equipment needed for cleaning and dishwashing duties Perform other duties required as needed Preferred Qualifications: Previous dishwashing experience preferred Superior customer service standards Ability to maintain a safe work environment Ability to multitask and work in a fast-paced environment Knowledge of, or ability to learn, standard cleaning methods and equipment used in dishwashing work Ability to understand and carry out oral and written instructions Ability to exert continuous physical effort including frequent bending, walking and heavy lifting Excellent interpersonal skills for communicating with fellow team members and customers Excellent attendance Benefits: Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits To apply for position, send cover letter and resume to: University of Charleston 2300 MacCorkle Avenue, SE, Charleston, WV\u00a0 25304 virginiamoore@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/food-service-worker/": {"title": "Food Service Worker", "description": "Food Service Worker - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Food Service Worker Food Service Worker Posted April 30, 2024 Food Service Worker Food Services, University of Charleston ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE POSTION: Prepare food for service using established procedures, and recipes Prepare and set up of food at an account and location Maintain clean, neat and orderly areas Complete daily duties/tasks within the scheduled work shift Maintain a fast pace and ability to multitask when performing duties Assist in the preparation of hot and/or cold foods, and properly stores food, utilizing knowledge of temperature requirements and spoilage Set up stations with entr\u00e9es, soups, salads, breads, condiments, other food products and utensils Interact with guests in the serving, retail and dining areas Follow proper guest service procedures whenever interacting with others by smiling, making eye contact and greeting guests Clean and sanitize workstations and equipment following all client and regulatory rules and procedures PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Customer oriented Previous food service experience a plus Strong work ethic Excellent communication skills Must be a team player Ability to lift up to 40 pounds as necessary Willing to work nights/weekends/overtime as needed Excellent attendance Benefits: Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits To apply for position, send cover letter and resume to: University of Charleston Elizabeth Brandt at elizabethbrandt@ucwv.edu Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/grounds-keeper/": {"title": "Grounds Keeper", "description": "Grounds Keeper - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Grounds Keeper Grounds Keeper Posted April 13, 2024 Grounds Keeper Facilities Department, University of Charleston JOB SUMMARY: Care for all grounds, trees, exterior components, and landscape. This includes but is not limited to mowing, trimming trees and shrubs, trash removal, flower planting and care, and weeding. A skill in operating landscape equipment is required.\u00a0 Driving off campus is necessary at times.\u00a0 Overtime work is mandatory at times in order to keep up with the activities and events on campus.\u00a0 This position will be expected to perform basic custodial work and other duties as assigned. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE POSITION: High School diploma or GED Capable of lifting 40 pounds, working with automated equipment, and operating an automobile on and off campus All candidates for employment must be able to pass a thorough background check and hold a clear driving record Ability to prioritize and organize effectively Ability to communicate effectively with the manager and associates Ability to work independently with little supervision Knowledge of general office procedures Flexible, resourceful, willing to learn\\cross-train Must be a team player Ability to work in extreme climates Ability to operate power equipment Other duties as assigned as needed Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume and references to: Jennifer McCallister jennifermccallister@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/grill-cook/": {"title": "Grill Cook", "description": "Grill Cook - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Grill Cook Grill Cook Posted April 4, 2024 Grill Cook Food Service & Catering,\u00a0University of Charleston Primary Functions: Responsible for customer service, food preparation, cooking to customer\u2019s order, and cleanliness of the dining location. Duties & Responsibilities: Cook and prepare menu items to customer\u2019s order Preparation of other food items directed by General Manager or Chef Maintains proper grill cooking temperatures Ensures proper sanitation of grill area and surrounding kitchen Uses proper portioning Answers customer questions accurately on menu items Restocks and cleans up grill station at end of service period Other duties as required and assigned Requirements: Able to read, write and perform basic math Able to follow verbal and written instructions Must be customer-oriented, organized and detail oriented Able to occasionally lift 30 pounds Must be able to move through the kitchen/grill area to retrieve/gather supplies and equipment Bending, standing, moving, carrying, writing, lifting, reaching High standard of personal hygiene Benefits: Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current resume to: Elizabeth Brandt at elizabethbrandt@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/cashier/": {"title": "Cashier", "description": "Cashier - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Cashier Cashier Posted April 4, 2024 Cashier Food Services,\u00a0University of Charleston Duties & Responsibilities: Operate a cash register efficiently and accurately Prepare products and order stock Ensure the proper signage when needed Maintain a level of excellence with a smile, through great service and small-talk with each customer you assist Maintain clean, neat, and orderly cash register and dining areas Able to lift/ transport 30lbs occasionally Perform other duties required as needed Requirements: Accurately record guest transactions Cashier experience a plus, but not required Ability to make correct change\u00a0and work in a fast-paced environment Excellent Attendance Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should a resume to: Elizabeth Brandt at elizabethbrandt@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift \u00a9 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"}, "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/cook-2/": {"title": "Cook", "description": "Cook - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Cook Cook Posted April 4, 2024 Cook Food Service & Catering,\u00a0University of Charleston Job Summary: The University of Charleston seeks a full-time Food Service employee to join the Culinary Team; previous cooking experience is required. Must be able to work weekends and nights as needed and shifts will vary. Essential Functions: Prepares recipes for meal periods Garnishes and places food items at the appropriate stations Ensures and maintains proper sanitation of the kitchen Uses proper portioning Answers customer questions accurately on menu items Assists in restocking and clean-up of the kitchen and serving stations at the end of the service period Other duties as assigned Preferred Qualifications: Must be able to read and follow recipes and follow directions. Experienced with general kitchen procedures Understands the importance of health department and AVI Fresh food and safety guidelines Must be a team player and perform well in meeting deadlines Ability to lift up to 40 pounds as necessary Willing to work nights/weekends/overtime as needed Must understand the importance of security and confidentiality associated with a university campus Excellent attendance Benefits: Health Insurance (Medical, Dental and Vision) Life Insurance 403(b) Retirement Plan Vacation Accrual Sick Accrual Paid Holidays Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Tuition Benefits Review of resumes will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current resume to: Virginia Moore virginiamoore@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information 